text: >-
  Blake Bednarz v

  @BlakeBednarz • 25m

  5 ...

  Charlie Kirk post ≥

  IMO No one will ever be able to recreate a gun shot

  where a necklace busts away while the t-shirt violently reverberates... All

  *BEFORE* there's any sign of a wound/blood. It's impossible! *IF* Charlie

  was actually shot, the 1st frame would & should show some degree of entry

  wound / blood / splatter from his neck! (In every experiment completed -

  there is visible evidence of a bullet entering their test subject during the

  initial frame). In CK's case, the initial frame is his shirt exploding & there
  is

  ZERO blood or splatter. The gush of blood comes from his neck multiple

  frames *AFTER* his t-shirt calms down from the strange reverberation &

  explosion. This was not a gun.

  *IF* they found a bullet inside Charlie's neck (per C.O.'s unnamed leak) -

  well, it was fired after he left UVU because a gun did not do what the world

  witnessed live on September 10 under the tent.

  I believe there was a detonation under Charlie's shirt which created a close

  proximity projectile in tandem with a strong shock (think taser like effect on

  his body causing that posture).

  TURNIN

  POINT

  MALE ANTID
